## Hints for Future Agents
The selector loss is an explicit TorchSpec design: teacher-forced cross-entropy over the base top-K candidates when the gold successor is present. Do not describe it as upstream training parity. DFlash2Config must be dispatched before DFlashConfig. Packed convolutions must reset at every block boundary. Official top-level num_target_layers is target depth, while TorchSpec uses num_target_layers as the captured-layer count.

